\paragraph{The rank endpoint and a point-concentration construction.}
Fix a nonzero cluster $E_\lambda$ of dimension $D$, with orthonormal basis $(\phi_j)_{j=1}^D$, and write
\[
 K(x,y)=\sum_{j=1}^D\phi_j(x)\overline{\phi_j(y)}.
\]
For any rank-$r$ subspace $Q\subset E_\lambda$, $1\leq r\leq D$, its density satisfies
$\int_M\rho_Q=r$.
At $p=2$ the source exponents give $s(2)=0$ and $\alpha(2)=1$, so this exactly equals the required lower bound. This endpoint is an identity, not new sharpness progress.

For any $x$ with $K(x,x)>0$, the vector
\[
 v_x(y)=K(y,x)/\sqrt{K(x,x)}
\]
has norm one and $|v_x(x)|^2=K(x,x)$. Extend it to an orthonormal $r$-tuple in $E_\lambda$ and let $Q_x$ be its span. The other vectors vanish at $x$: their inner product with $K(\cdot,x)$ is their evaluation at $x$, up to the chosen inner-product convention. Consequently
\[
 \rho_{Q_x}(x)=K(x,x),\qquad
 \max_{\substack{Q\subset E_\lambda\\\dim Q=r}}\rho_Q(x)=K(x,x).
\]
The upper bound follows by extending a basis of $Q$ to one of $E_\lambda$ and dropping nonnegative terms. Since $\int_M K(x,x)=D$, some point has $K(x,x)\geq D/\operatorname{vol}(M)$. We obtain $\|\rho_{Q_x}\|_\infty\geq D/\operatorname{vol}(M)$ for every allowed rank.

\paragraph{Comparison with the desired frequency scale.}
At $p=\infty$, the requested scale is $\lambda^{n-1}$, independent of $r$, because $2s(\infty)=n-1$ and $1/\alpha(\infty)=0$. The preceding construction reaches that scale on any chosen sequence satisfying the additional estimate $D\geq c_0\lambda^{n-1}$. We have not proved that estimate for the source's frequency windows, and the intermediate-rank assumption alone does not imply it. The construction applies without it but gives only the stated bound in terms of $D$.

\paragraph{Why endpoints do not fill the gap.}
Large value at one point does not bound the volume on which the density is large. For $2<p<\infty$, that volume and the arrangement of $r$ orthogonal modes determine the $L^{p/2}$ norm. Interpolation of upper bounds cannot supply a missing lower bound. A construction with quantified spatial concentration and the specified rank scaling is still required on general compact manifolds. The source-known two-sphere result is retained rather than replaced by these endpoint identities.

